From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blackhat-7 <44942105+blackhat-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 05:05:14 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 06/33] MTP drafting: cumulative draft stop, draft-head context
 rows, the draft kernel diet, no residual copy, fused final mixer

Port of opt7/integrate 4c974469 c72d75a8 80a7262d 0a4ce888 (draft stop, context rows) and b520153b 891f28c3
8a452759 af57e5fd 6fcd6bac 15b36108 204d7f78 d4653e9d 49635320 10ce334d (diet) onto v0.2.9. One commit: the levers
share MtpDrafter's graphs and the head kernels.
- STRATA_SPEC_CUM=S (+ STRATA_SPEC_CUM_ACC table, STRATA_SPEC_CUM_ADAPT): an MTP window keeps drafts while the
  estimated chance that all hold stays >= S (strata/spec/draft_cum.hpp); MtpDrafter::draft stops at the same draft.
  Serve and generate loops of v0.2.9 (the classic path; the gated path needs --pcie-frac 0, not ported).
  STRATA_SPEC_LOG=<file>: a line per window (generate).
- STRATA_MTP_CTX_ROWS=N: draft head rows for prompt/text tokens the draft vocabulary lacks; kept with v0.2.9's
  cross-card draft head gather.
- STRATA_MTP_FUSE (default on gfx1100): the draft graphs in fewer launches, the same drafts and probabilities;
  multi-block head ops and the fused norm+rope on gfx1100 (verify_parity, rope_parity on HIP).
- STRATA_MTP_NO_RCOPY, STRATA_MTP_MIX_FUSED (opt-in, set by the run config; MIX_FUSED moves draft probabilities in
  their last bits, drafts only).
- Our STRATA_MTP_STAMPS dropped: v0.2.9's own stage profile (g_mp) covers it.
Measured on 0.1.43: draft stop code +3.7-4.6%, edit +3.7-5.3%, prose +1-2%; diet -0.15..-1.1 ms a round; no-rcopy
and mixer 1.92 -> 1.78 ms a round.
